  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "BER: prevent possible signed overlow undefined behavior",
  "description": "In a ASN.1 CHOICE, it's possible for the CHOICE length to be\nlarger than that of the chosen child item. dissect_ber_choice\ndoesn't dissect the leftover bytes in that case, but always\nreturns the end offset based on the outer length.\n\nThat can overflow in the case where the tvb passed into\ndissect_ber_choice is a subset of some other tvb, and it's added\nlater, which happens in SPNEGO and other protocols that call\nKerberos. To be safe, call ensure_reported_length_remaining,\nwhich will throw the same exception as would be thrown if the\nbytes up to that offset were dissected. (It does not throw an\nexception if the offset is right at the end of the buffer.)\nThis prevents overflow and also causes invalid BER to produce\nan error.\n\nOSS-Fuzz Issue 456050170",
  "state": "merged",
